            <ArticleTitle>[Angel-shaped phalango-epiphyseal dysplasia: case report].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e1-e4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.5546/aap.2017.e1</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe a rare and sporadic condition, characterized by swan neck deformity in hands, hip osteoarthritis in adulthood and malformations of the middle phalanges with an angel shape. The patient is a 4 year old boy who suffered hand trauma and on x-ray examination he was diagnosed with angel-shaped phalango-epiphyseal dysplasia. Based on this diagnosis, his mother, who suffered from constant pain in her hips and lower limbs, was diagnosed with this syndrome as well.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>Sociedad Argentina de Pediatría.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
